    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          The best dehumidifier for a basement with a floor drain is one you connect to a hose and forget. Gravity drainage is cheap, silent and has nothing to fail, but it only works when the drain is lower than the dehumidifier's port, and the details matter: whether a hose is in the box, whether the port takes a garden hose, how high it sits and where the water ends up. This guide picks seven units with good drain designs and explains how to set them up.
        </p>

