        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most basements with a floor drain, the Midea Cube 50 is the dehumidifier with a drain hose to buy: the hose is in the box, it drains by gravity and its oversized tank covers you if the drain ever clogs. If your drain is farther away, the Frigidaire FHDD5034Y1's garden hose port lets you buy exactly the length you need, and the conventional Midea MAD50C1AWS-A is the budget pick.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever you choose, start with the drain: make sure it is below the port, keep the hose short and sloping downhill with no loops, test it before you walk away and flush it once or twice a season. If the water has to go up, buy a pump rather than a longer hose.
          </p>
